{"path":"numeric/complex/conj","title":"conjf, conj, conjl","titleHtml":"conjf, conj, conjl","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/complex/conj","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"The complex conjugate of z.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex\"><code>&lt;complex.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; conjf<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;conj<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> conjl<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/tgmath\"><code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define conj( z )</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> Computes the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_conjugate\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">complex conjugate</a> of <code>z</code> by reversing the sign of the imaginary part.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Type-generic macro: if <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/imaginary\"><span class=\"kw745\">imaginary</span></a></span></code>, or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span></code>, <code>conjl</code> is called. If <code>z</code>  has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/imaginary\"><span class=\"kw745\">imaginary</span></a></span></code>, or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span></span></code>, <code>conjf</code> is called. If <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/imaginary\"><span class=\"kw745\">imaginary</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span></code>, or any integer type, <code>conj</code> is called.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  complex argument\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The complex conjugate of <code>z</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>On C99 implementations that do not implement <span class=\"t-lc\">I</span> as <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/Imaginary_I\">_Imaginary_I</a></span>, <code>conj</code> may be used to obtain complex numbers with negative zero imaginary part. In C11, the macro <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/CMPLX\">CMPLX</a></span> is used for that purpose.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>I<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> conj<span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw848\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"The conjugate of&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi is&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>,\n            <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw848\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Their product is&nbsp;%.1f%+.1fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"sy2\">*</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"sy2\">*</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>The conjugate of 1.0+2.0i is 1.0-2.0i\nTheir product is 5.0+0.0i</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.9.4 The conj functions (p: 198)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 373-375)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.7 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 545)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.9.3 The conj functions (p: 179)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.22 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 335-337)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.7 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 480)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>conj</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table></div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"Complex number arithmetic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"conjf, conj, conjl","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations. Computes the complex conjugate of z by reversing the sign of the imaginary part."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The complex conjugate of z."},{"label":"Notes","note":"On C99 implementations that do not implement I as _Imaginary_I, conj may be used to obtain complex numbers with negative zero imaginary part."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":255,"codeBlockCount":2}
